# Atheros QCA6174 (168c:003e) on the Coral Dev Board, reached over pcie0.
# The part reports no subsystem ids, so board-2.bin cannot match it and
# ath10k falls back to the generic board.bin - keep the whole directory
# rather than guessing which files the driver will ask for.
ath10k/QCA6174/hw3.0/*

# QCA6174 bluetooth, the other half of the same combo part, on uart2.
# btqca builds the names from the controller version it reads out of the
# chip (btqca.c:850,944 - "qca/rampatch_%08x.bin" and "qca/nvm_%08x.bin").
# The chip reports 0x00440302:
#   Bluetooth: hci0: QCA controller version 0x00440302
# Do not infer this from the vendor rootfs. It ships the 00130302 pair and
# a rampatch_tlv_3.2.tlv symlink pointing at it, but that is what the old
# downstream driver used; mainline asks for a different file.
qca/*00440302*.bin
